            {
              "title": "Querying available models via API",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The catalog above is a snapshot: it changes whenever Anthropic releases or retires models. `GET /v1/models` returns the list of models enabled for your API key at request time, instead of relying on a fixed table in your code or on this page."
                },
                {
                  "type": "code",
                  "language": "bash",
                  "code": "curl https://api.anthropic.com/v1/models \\\n  -H \"x-api-key: $ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"anthropic-version: 2023-06-01\""
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "It makes sense to use it when:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "cards",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "icon": "🔀",
                      "title": "Dynamic selector",
                      "description": "Populate a model dropdown in an admin UI without hardcoding or redeploying every time a new model ships."
                    },
                    {
                      "icon": "✅",
                      "title": "Validate before pinning an ID",
                      "description": "Confirm that a model ID is still current before saving it to configuration, instead of discovering in production that it was retired."
                    },
                    {
                      "icon": "🔔",
                      "title": "Detect new models",
                      "description": "A periodic job that checks whether a newer model appeared, without relying on manually reading the changelog."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "style": "info",
                  "title": "Not needed for normal use",
                  "content": "To simply call Claude with a known model, `GET /models` isn't necessary — the `model` is passed directly in `POST /messages`. This endpoint matters only when the catalog itself is part of the application logic (dynamic selection, validation, availability monitoring)."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
